          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#References"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#superfluid_dark_matter"} Superfluid dark matter
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#mond_phenomenology"} MOND Phenomenology
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesTensionWithHydrogenLineSpectroscopy"} Comparison and tension with experiment
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A model for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+matter"} dark matter
            made up of massive but extremely light
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Broglie+wavelength"} de Broglie wavelength
            is at the scale of galaxies.
          %p
            The idea is that on scales above that of galaxies, the predictions of fuzzy dark matter agree with the standard cold dark matter models that work exceptionally well on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmological scales
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum
            properties of these light particles become relevant and change their effect just so as to fix the problems (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MOND"} MOND
          %p
            A natural candidate for such ultra-light particles are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axions"} axions
          %p
            This kind of model was brought up independently by several groups of authors (see
            %a{:href => "#Lee17"} Lee 17
            for historical survey) with early precursors going back as far as (
            %a{:href => "#BaldeschiGelminiRuffini83"}> Baldeschi-Gelmini-Ruffini 83
            ), and accordingly goes by a number of different names, including the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bose-Einstein+condensate"} Bose-Einstein condensate
                  (BEC) dark matter
                (
                %a{:href => "#Sin92"}> Sin 92
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#SikivieYang09"} Sikivie-Yang 09
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfluid"} superfluid
                  dark matter
                (
                %a{:href => "#BerezhianiKhoury15"}> Berezhiani-Khoury 15
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#Khoury16"} Khoury 16
            %li
              %p
                %em fuzzy dark matter
                (
                %a{:href => "#WuBarkanaGruzinov00"}> Wu-Barkana-Gruzinov 00
                )
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  ultra-light
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axion"} axion
                (
                %a{:href => "#ErkenSikivieTamYang12"}> Erken-Sikivie-Tam-Yang 12
                )
            %li
              %p
                %em wave dark matter
            %li
              %p
                %em repulsive dark matter
          %p and more.
          %p
            The suggestion that fuzzy dark matter induces the observed almost-flat galactic rotation curves (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MOND"}> MOND
            ”) seems to go back to (
            %a{:href => "#Sin92"}> Sin 92
            ). Further pointers are in (
            %a{:href => "#Lee17"}> Lee 17, p. 3
            ):
          %blockquote
            %p There are many works explaining the rotation curves of dwarf [17, 23, 69], and large galaxies [29, 43, 70–78] in this model.
          %p
            More recently, detection of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/21cm+hydrogen+line"} 21cm hydrogen line
            from cosmic dawn indicates that star formation set in earlier than compatible with fuzzy dark matter models (
            %a{:href => "#Nebrin17"}> Nebrin 17
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#NebrinGharaMellema18"} Nebrin-Ghara-Mellema 18
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p Early precursors of the idea include
          %ul
            %li#BaldeschiGelminiRuffini83 M. R. Baldeschi, G. B. Gelmini, and R. Ruffini, Physics Letters B 122, 221 (1983).
          %p
            The role of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bose-Einstein+condensate"} Bose-Einstein condensate
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axions"} axions
            on galactic scales was considered in
          %ul
            %li#Sin92
              %p
                Sang-Jin Sin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Late time Cosmological Phase Transition and Galactic Halo as Bose-liquid
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9205208"} arXiv:hep-ph/9205208
            %li#SikivieYang09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Sikivie"}> Pierre Sikivie
                , Q. Yang,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bose-Einstein Condensation of Dark Matter Axions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.1106"} arXiv:0901.1106
            %li#ErkenSikivieTamYang12
              %p
                O. Erken,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Sikivie"} Pierre Sikivie
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmic axion thermalization
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.1157"} arXiv:1111.1157
          %p The proposal in the guise of “fuzzy dark matter” is originally due to
          %ul
            %li#WuBarkanaGruzinov00
              Wayne Hu, Rennan Barkana, Andrei Gruzinov,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cold and Fuzzy Dark Matter
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/0003365"} arXiv:astro-ph/0003365
          %p A detailed discussion is in
          %ul
            %li#HOTW16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lam+Hui"}> Lam Hui
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeremiah+Ostriker"} Jeremiah Ostriker
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Tremaine"} Scott Tremaine
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the hypothesis that cosmological dark matter is composed of ultra-light bosons
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.08297"} arXiv:1610.08297
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                David J. E. Marsh,
                %em Axion Cosmology
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1510.07633"}> arXiv:1510.07633
                )
            %li#Lee17
              %p
                Jae-Weon Lee,
                %em Brief History of Ultra-light Scalar Dark Matter Models
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.05057"}> arXiv:1704.05057
                )
            %li
              %p
                Luca Visinelli:
                %em Axions as Dark Matter, Dark Energy, and Dark Radiation
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.17059"}> arXiv:2509.17059
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Computer simulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+formation"} structure formation
            with fuzzy dark matter:
          %ul
            %li
              Philip Mocz et al.,
              = succeed "," do
                %em First Star-Forming Structures in Fuzzy Cosmic Filaments
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.141301"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.141301
          %p
            Some thoughts on the quantum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurement+problem"} measurement problem
            for fuzzy DM particles with huge macroscopic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Compton+wavelengths"} Compton wavelengths
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Adam D. Helfer,
              %em Quantum measurement and fuzzy dark matter
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.04946"}> arXiv:1809.04946
              )
          %h3#superfluid_dark_matter Superfluid dark matter
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfluid"} superfluid
            dark matter:
          %ul
            %li#HossenfelderMistele19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sabine+Hossenfelder"}> Sabine Hossenfelder
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Mistele"} Tobias Mistele
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Strong lensing with superfluid dark matter
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1475-7516/2019/02/001"} doi:10.1088/1475-7516/2019/02/001
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.00840"} arXiv:1809.00840
            %li#Mistele22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Mistele"}> Tobias Mistele
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stacy+McGaugh"} Stacy McGaugh
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sabine+Hossenfelder"} Sabine Hossenfelder
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Galactic mass-to-light ratios with superfluid dark matter
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202243216"} doi:10.1051/0004-6361/202243216
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.07282"} arXiv:2201.07282
            %li
              %p
                Giordano Cintia, Valerio De Luca,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Khoury"} Justin Khoury
                %em Superfluid Dark Matter
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.23900"}> arXiv:2505.23900
                \&amp;rbrack; ,
          %h3#mond_phenomenology MOND Phenomenology
          %p
            Discussion of how
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfluid"} superfluid
            aspects of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axion"} axionic
            fuzzy dark matter reproduce
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MOND"} MOND
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BerezhianiKhoury15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lasha+Berezhiani"}> Lasha Berezhiani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Khoury"} Justin Khoury
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theory of Dark Matter Superfluidity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.01019"} arXiv:1507.01019
            %li#Khoury16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Khoury"}> Justin Khoury
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Another Path for the Emergence of Modified Galactic Dynamics from Dark Matter Superfluidity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.05961"} arXiv:1602.05961
            %li
              %p
                JiJi Fan,
                %em Ultralight Repulsive Dark Matter and BEC
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.06580"}> arXiv:1603.06580
                )
            %li
              %p
                Andrea Addazi, Antonino Marciano,
                %em UV completion of a theory of Superfluid Dark Matter
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.04083"}> arXiv:1801.04083
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Khoury"}> Justin Khoury
                ,
                %em Dark Matter Superfluidity
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.10928"}> arXiv:2109.10928
                )
          %h3#ReferencesTensionWithHydrogenLineSpectroscopy Comparison and tension with experiment
          %p
            Comparison to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            (observation):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Bohua Li, Tanja Rindler-Daller, and Paul R. Shapiro,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmological constraints on Bose-Einstein-condensed scalar field dark matter
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.6061"} arXiv:1310.6061
            %li
              %p
                Hsi-Yu Schive, Tzihong Chiueh, Tom Broadhurst,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmic structure as the quantum interference of a coherent dark wave
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.nature.com/nphys/journal/v10/n7/abs/nphys2996.html"} doi:10.1038/nphys2996
            %li
              %p
                Nilanjan Banik, Adam J. Christopherson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Sikivie"} Pierre Sikivie
                = succeed "," do
                  %em New astrophysical bounds on ultralight axionlike particles
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.04573"} arXiv:1701.04573
          %p
            Strong constraints on fuzzy dark matter from observation of the cosmic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/21cm+hydrogen+line"} 21cm hydrogen line
            are claimed and discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Adam Lidz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lam+Hui"} Lam Hui
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Implications of a Pre-reionization 21 cm Absorption Signal for Fuzzy Dark Matter
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.01253"} arXiv:1805.01253
            %li#Nebrin17
              %p
                Olof Nebrin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmic Dawn in a Fuzzy Universe: Constraining the nature of Dark Matterwith 21 cm Cosmology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.diva-portal.org/smash/record.jsf?pid=diva2%3A1195402&dswid=-8037"} diva2:1195402
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://su.diva-portal.org/smash/record.jsf?pid=diva2%3A1195402&dswid=6755"} urn:nbn:se:su:diva-154861
            %li#NebrinGharaMellema18
              %p
                Olof Nebrin, Raghunath Ghara, Garrelt Mellema,
                %em Fuzzy Dark Matter at Cosmic Dawn: New 21-cm Constraints
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.09760"}> arXiv:1812.09760
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.reddit.com/r/Physics/comments/a9zeeb/my_first_paper_fuzzy_dark_matter_at_cosmic_dawn/"} reddit
          %p
            Claim that the galaxy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core-cusp+problem"} core-cusp problem
            is not resolved after all is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Heling Deng, Mark P. Hertzberg, Mohammad Hossein Namjoo, Ali Masoumi,
              %em Can Light Dark Matter Solve the Core-Cusp Problem?
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.05921"}> arXiv:1804.05921
              )
          %p
            Claim that the fitting of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/galaxy+rotation+curves"} galaxy rotation curves
            is not resolved after all:
          %ul
            %li
              Mariangela Lisanti, Matthew Moschella, Nadav Joseph Outmezguine, Oren Slone,
              %em The Inconsistency of Superfluid Dark Matter with Milky Way Dynamics
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.12365"}> arXiv:1911.12365
              )
          %p Claim that superfluid dark matter is in tension with weak gravitational lensing data:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Mistele"}> Tobias Mistele
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stacy+McGaugh"} Stacy McGaugh
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sabine+Hossenfelder"} Sabine Hossenfelder
              %em Superfluid dark matter in tension with weak gravitational lensing data
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.08560"}> arXiv:2303.08560
              )
